.TH LAMP 1 "2026-08-05" "lamp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lamp \- control the Mi Bedside Lamp 2 over the local network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lamp
[\fIargument\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls a Mi Bedside Lamp 2 (MJCTD02YL) directly over the miIO protocol on
udp/54321. Everything happens on the local network: there is no cloud round
trip, no hub, and no dependency on the Xiaomi or Yeelight apps. The lamp's
HomeKit pairing is untouched, so the Home app keeps working alongside it.
.PP
Setting a brightness or colour on a lamp that is off will also turn it on.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B (none)
Toggle power.
.TP
.BR on ", " off
Set power directly.
.TP
.B <0-100>
Set brightness as a percentage. A value of 0 turns the lamp off.
.TP
.BI <n> k
Set colour temperature in kelvin, for example
.BR "lamp 2700k" .
Values are clamped to the 1700\-6500K the device accepts. The
.B k
suffix is required, so that brightness and temperature cannot be confused.
.TP
.BR warm ", " cool
Shorthand for 2700k and 5000k.
.TP
.BI # rrggbb
Set colour. The leading hash is optional.
.TP
.BI @ scene
Apply a named scene from the configuration file.
.TP
.B status
Print power, brightness, and current colour or temperature.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lamp/config.toml
Device address, token, and scene definitions. Contains a device credential and
should be mode 600.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.EX
ip = "192.168.1.4"
token = "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"

[scenes.read]
brightness = 80
kelvin = 4000

[scenes.sleep]
brightness = 5
rgb = "#ff3000"
.EE
.PP
The token is a 32 character hex string, obtained once from the Xiaomi cloud
account the lamp is registered to.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits non-zero if the configuration is missing or invalid, if the argument is
not understood, or if the lamp does not answer. A lamp that is switched off at
the wall is reported as unreachable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swatch (1)
